  "title": "Erdős Problem #169",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $k\\geq 3$ and $f(k)$ be the supremum of $\\sum_{n\\in A}\\frac{1}{n}$ as $A$ ranges over all sets of positive integers which do not contain a $k$-term arithmetic progression. Estimate $f(k)$.\nIs $ \\lim_{k\\to \\infty}\\frac{f(k)}{\\log W(k)}=\\infty $ where $W(k)$ is the van der Waerden number?",
